# Cannelloni License & Terms of Use

Cannelloni is an open-source, lightweight retro gaming launcher and libretro frontend designed for Linux handheld devices.

---

## 1. Upstream Code & Original Ownership

Cannelloni is a fork and continuation of **MinUI** (originally developed by Shaun Inman) and draws conceptual inspiration from **Cannoli** (developed by CannoliHQ).

The maintainer of this fork (Denarmo) is **not** the original owner or creator of the underlying upstream codebase. All original rights, copyrights, and intellectual property from upstream projects belong to their respective creators:

- **MinUI Frontend & Framework**:
  Copyright (c) Shaun Inman and MinUI Contributors.
  Original Repository: https://github.com/shauninman/MinUI
  All original MinUI code remains credited to Shaun Inman and contributors.

- **Cannoli Frontend Inspiration**:
  Copyright (c) CannoliHQ and Cannoli Contributors.
  Original Repository: https://github.com/CannoliHQ/cannoli

- **Third-Party Cores, Toolchains, and Libraries**:
  All bundled emulators, Libretro cores (including melonDS, DeSmuME, PCSX ReARMed, Snes9x, mGBA, Nestopia, Gambatte, Genesis Plus GX, FBNeo, etc.), SDL, FreeType, libpng, and device-specific utilities are copyrighted by their respective authors and licensed under their original licenses (GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, LGPL, MIT, or custom permissive licenses as noted in their source trees).

